if (is_partial_io(bvec))
    kfree(uncmem);
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that `kunmap_atomic(user_mem)` is only called when the operation is not a partial I/O, preventing access to an unmapped page. It also correctly handles the freeing of `uncmem` only in the context of partial writes, ensuring that memory is not freed prematurely, thus preventing invalid memory references during disk write operations.

